#reference: Sputtering Yields, Wolfgang Eckstein, 2007
##the fitting formula of sputtering yield have some errors which was corrected at ftp://ftp.rzg.mpg.de/pub/ipp/eckstein/rep05/errors_chapter4.pdf
##this corrected file can also be found on:https://drive.google.com/file/d/11pF82xcbjxDqihPpzr35OjzNzaTHaMYB/view?usp=sharing
##these fitting parameters are used for computing Sputtered energy coefficient
#fitting parameters for Eckstein physical sputtering yield.
#the fitting formular is valid when: for low mass ions, the maximum incident energy is 20keV
##for heavy ions, the maximum incident energy is 200keV. 
#for each material, and each incident species, the fitting parameters for different incident species are different.
##:first column: incident species name;
##:second column: target species name;
##:third column: lambda;
##:fourth column: q;
##:fifth column: mu;
##:sixth column: the threshold energy;
##:seventh column: the energy at Lindhard screening length(\varepsilon)
##:eighth column: the surface binding energy(in unit eV) 
##:ninth column: E_sb/gamma
##:tenth column: max yield
##:eleventh column: energy of max yield(in unit eV)
##:twelfth column: angle of max yield

